  "published": "2026-11-01T11:29:20.94Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.1.0: MediatR compatibility. Changes from 2.0.0 that need attention are marked \"Breaking\"; 2.0.0 was published the day before and had no downloads.\n- Breaking: Publish re-throws handler and sink failures, as MediatR does. Every sink still runs; one failure is re-thrown as is, several as an AggregateException. The dependency on Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions is removed.\n- Breaking: two handlers for the same request make AddAnyMediator throw an InvalidOperationException naming both classes. Before, the first one found was used silently.\n- Breaking: ISender gains Send(object) and IPublisher gains Publish(object), as in MediatR. Classes that implement these interfaces by hand must add them.\n- Handlers for a base class or interface of a notification also receive it (INotificationHandler<IDomainEvent> runs for every IDomainEvent). A handler class runs once per Publish.\n- Open generic request and notification handlers are found by scanning and closed when a message is dispatched, e.g. GetByIdHandler<T> : IRequestHandler<GetById<T>, T>.\n- IPipelineBehavior and IStreamPipelineBehavior constrain TRequest to notnull, as MediatR does, so behaviors written for MediatR compile unchanged.\n- cfg.TypeEvaluator filters the types registered by scanning, as in MediatR.",
